<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    dmux durable per-host policy loader (ADR 012 WS-F.1; plan §21 steps 7
    and 9; ADR 010 §5). `launchctl setenv` does not survive a reboot: Macie
    lost its canary flag exactly that way on 2026-08-19. This one-shot agent
    (RunAtLoad, no KeepAlive) re-applies every KEY=VALUE of the untracked,
    host-local ~/.config/dmux/service.env with `launchctl setenv` at each
    login, which is where the WezTerm GUI reads DMUX_WEZ_FIRST when it is
    launched (shared/wezterm/wezterm.lua:9). The mux job does not depend on
    this agent's order: dmux-mux-start.sh reads the same file itself.
    The file's grammar and whole-file refusal rules live in
    shared/wezterm/mux/dmux-service-env.sh; the program is dmux-env-load.sh.

    Install, once, after `dotfile link` has placed this file:
      launchctl bootstrap gui/$UID ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.fredrir.dmux-env.plist
    Re-apply after editing service.env (then restart the mux, which kills
    its panes, and relaunch the GUI):
      launchctl kickstart gui/$UID/com.fredrir.dmux-env
    Inspect: `launchctl print gui/$UID/com.fredrir.dmux-env` (a nonzero last
    exit status means the file was refused whole and nothing was applied),
    `launchctl getenv DMUX_WEZ_FIRST`, and `dmux doctor`, which reports the
    process, launchd and file layers side by side.
    This job only sets; it never unsets. Write DMUX_WEZ_FIRST=0 to state
    legacy (ADR 010 §5) rather than deleting the line: since the §21 step 9
    flip a file that states no DMUX_WEZ_FIRST (or no file at all) makes this
    job place the tracked default DMUX_WEZ_FIRST=1 in the session.
  -->
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.fredrir.dmux-env</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/Users/fredrir/dotfiles/shared/wezterm/mux/dmux-env-load.sh</string>
  </array>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>
  <key>ProcessType</key>
  <string>Background</string>
  <!-- No StandardOutPath/StandardErrorPath, for the same reason as
       com.fredrir.wezterm-mux: asking launchd to open predictable /tmp log
       paths follows a preplanted symlink. The loader mirrors its messages to
       the unified log through `logger` instead. -->
</dict>
</plist>
